From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:30:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 200/342] usb_webcam: YUY2 with NEON, unplug and replug, killed
 consumers (M45)

YUY2 to B_RGB32 goes through NEON on arm64 (yuy2_neon.c), bit for bit
the same: a 640x480 frame takes a Cortex-A53 1.4 ms instead of 6.3.

Unplugging the camera while it streamed would have crashed the
media_addon_server: BUSBRoster deletes the device right after
DeviceRemoved(), and the data pump went on using its endpoint. Now:
- usb_raw cancels the transfers of every interface when its device is
  removed (only the first one's were, and a webcam streams on its
  second: the pipes going later drop them without calling back, so a
  waiter hung);
- CamDevice::Unplugged() waits for the pump before the device goes, and
  the UVC code refuses a device that is gone.
A camera plugged in again goes to the node whose one was unplugged,
with that node's flavor ID: it stays the default video input, and a
connected application gets pictures again without restarting anything.

A camera plugged in after boot got no node, and none at all if none was
there at boot: the media_addon_server unloads an add-on without nodes,
and with it usb_webcam's USB roster. It now keeps an add-on that wants
to be autostarted loaded (usb_webcam says so and starts nothing; the
mixer, the other one, always has a node), and instantiates the
physical inputs and outputs of flavors that come later, then rescans
the defaults.

A consumer whose team died without disconnecting (CodyCam killed) left
the camera streaming and the output taken: the frame generator now
tells the node when the consumer's port is gone, and it disconnects.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
